SELECT '8d525eea-4922-7706-9628-69fec692e62c', 'a7217cfa-0c66-7bae-871a-25fe0124578a', 'Search in Rotated Sorted Array', 'Search in Rotated Sorted Array', 'Difficulty: Medium · LeetCode 33
Problem
Given array nums rotated at an unknown pivot and integer target, return index of target or -1 in $O(\log n)$ time.
Understanding the problem
At least one half of the array (left or right) is guaranteed to be strictly sorted at any step.
Intuition
Check if nums[left] <= nums[mid]. If True, left half is sorted: check if target is inside [nums[left], nums[mid]). Else right half is sorted: check if target is inside (nums[mid], nums[right]].
Approach
Set left = 0, right = len(nums) - 1.
Loop while left <= right:
If nums[mid] == target, return mid.
If nums[left] <= nums[mid] (Left half sorted):
If nums[left] <= target < nums[mid], move right = mid - 1; else left = mid + 1.
Else (Right half sorted):
If nums[mid] < target <= nums[right], move left = mid + 1; else right = mid - 1.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
Linear scan checking each element.
class Solution:
    def search(self, nums, target):

        for i, num in enumerate(nums):
            if num == target:
                return i

        return -1
class Solution {
public:
    int search(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {
            if (nums[i] == target) {
                return i;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
};
class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            if (nums[i] == target) {
                return i;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
}
var search = function(nums, target) {
    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
        if (nums[i] === target) {
            return i;
        }
    }

    return -1;
};
Time: O(n) · Space: O(1)
Optimized Code (Python 3)
class Solution:
    def search(self, nums, target):

        left = 0
        right = len(nums) - 1

        while left <= right:

            mid = left + (right - left) // 2

            if nums[mid] == target:
                return mid

            # Left half is sorted
            if nums[left] <= nums[mid]:

                if nums[left] <= target < nums[mid]:
                    right = mid - 1
                else:
                    left = mid + 1

            # Right half is sorted
            else:

                if nums[mid] < target <= nums[right]:
                    left = mid + 1
                else:
                    right = mid - 1

        return -1
