INSERT INTO "notes"."NoteSearchDocument" ("noteId", "versionId", "title", "topics", "body", "document", "updatedAt")
SELECT 'd85ffc37-108d-73bf-8b1a-ed908281f9fd', '87e97a44-df4e-7817-a930-3235ba8f380b', 'Pow(x, n)', 'Pow(x, n)', 'Difficulty: Medium · LeetCode 50
Problem
Implement pow(x, n) — raise x to the power n. n may be negative.
Understanding the problem
Multiplying x by itself n times is O(n). Binary exponentiation observes that x^n = (x²)^(n/2), halving the exponent each step — this gives O(log n).
Intuition
If n is even: x^n = (x²)^(n//2) — square x and halve n. If n is odd: multiply the current x into result first, then halve. Negative n → invert x.
Approach
If n < 0: set x = 1/x, n = -n.
Initialize result = 1.
While n > 0: if n % 2 == 1, multiply result *= x.
Square: x *= x; halve: n //= 2.
Return result.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
Multiply x by itself n times in a loop.
class Solution:
    def myPow(self, x, n):
        if n < 0:
            x = 1 / x
            n = -n

        result = 1

        for _ in range(n):
            result *= x

        return result
class Solution {
public:
    double myPow(double x, int n) {
        long long N = n;  // -n overflows int when n == INT_MIN
        if (N < 0) {
            x = 1 / x;
            N = -N;
        }

        double result = 1;

        for (long long i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            result *= x;
        }

        return result;
    }
};
class Solution {
    public double myPow(double x, int n) {
        long N = n;  // -n overflows int when n == Integer.MIN_VALUE
