INSERT INTO "notes"."NoteSearchDocument" ("noteId", "versionId", "title", "topics", "body", "document", "updatedAt")
SELECT '8358ecd9-bd59-78b0-8395-c2a3b2be10f2', '44b84ff1-2664-7d93-9541-2c566f727bc6', 'Diameter of Binary Tree', 'Diameter of Binary Tree', 'Difficulty: Easy · LeetCode 543
Problem
Given the root of a binary tree, return the length of the diameter of the tree (longest path between any two nodes).
Understanding the problem
The longest path passing through node u is left_height + right_height. The overall diameter is the max of this value across all nodes.
Intuition
Calculate height and diameter in the same bottom-up DFS traversal.
Approach
Initialize diameter = 0.
Define dfs(node): if node is None return 0.
Get left = dfs(node.left) and right = dfs(node.right).
Update diameter = max(diameter, left + right).
Return node height: 1 + max(left, right).
Naive Solution
For every node, separately calculate the height of its left and right subtree.
class Solution:
    def diameterOfBinaryTree(self, root):

        def height(node):
            if not node:
