Non-blocking Asynchronous I/O (Event Loop / Reactor Pattern): Used in Node.js, Nginx, Netty. A single thread (or one thread per core) multiplexes thousands of active connections using OS event notifications (such as `epoll` on Linux or `kqueue` on macOS). Instead of blocking a thread while waiting on disk/network I/O, the thread registers a callback and instantly moves to the next request. When I/O finishes, the OS raises an event and the thread executes the callback.'), 'C'),
  TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-07 03:23:53+00'
